    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000032a', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000065', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000329', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P3, category dependency, 1 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 1 runbook match(es), 0 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 1 service(s) over 139 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 2 evidence items; 0 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Few strong signals found; asking the planner for up to three extra read-only queries"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 1 direct, 0 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-11 05:25:00.000000', '2026-11-11 07:44:00.000000', '2026-11-11 03:06:00.000000', '2026-11-11 05:25:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P3", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "dependency", "candidate_service_names": ["benefits-portal"], "incident_summary": "Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS): benefits portal slow and intermittently unavailable. Users and systems of Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["benefits portal slow and intermittently unavailable"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P3", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P3"}', N'The benefits portal is slow or unavailable because our vendor is having a service problem in the Asia-Pacific region. We are tracking the vendor''s incident and will update employees when it is resolved.', N'Employees cannot reliably open the benefits portal of Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS); Keigan''s synthetic probe fails about 40 percent of the time with HTTP 503.', N'The SaaS vendor is experiencing degraded performance in its APAC region, which its status page confirms, and our probes see HTTP 503 and multi-second latency. No MetLife change is involved.', N'Nothing can be fixed on the Keigan side; track the vendor incident, inform employees and agree an ETA.

**Step 1. Track the vendor incident** (mitigate; low risk)

Subscribe to the vendor status page incident and share the link with the incident channel.

No check was given for this step.

**Step 2. Tell employees** (mitigate; low risk)

Post a banner or intranet notice that enrolment may be slow or unavailable.

No check was given for this step.

**Step 3. Open a vendor ticket** (mitigate; low risk)

Open a priority ticket with the vendor support channel quoting the synthetic probe failure times.

Check: Synthetic probes succeed.

Expected: Three consecutive runs succeed.', N'["What ETA has the vendor committed to?", "Should enrolment deadlines be extended while the vendor recovers?"]', N'{"schema_version": 2, "overview_markdown": "Nothing can be fixed on the Keigan side; track the vendor incident, inform employees and agree an ETA.", "step_references": [{"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-1"}, {"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-2"}, {"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-3"}]}', 0.9, NULL, N'{"nodes": [{"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000068", "serviceName": "benefits-portal", "serviceType": "saas_service", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "direct"}], "edges": [], "impactedSlos": [{"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002ad", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002ab", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000065", "applicationName": "Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS)", "serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000068", "serviceName": "benefits-portal", "sliName": "benefits-portal: Synthetic availability", "sliKind": "availability", "isHeadline": true, "isApproximate": false, "targetPercentage": 99.95, "rollingWindowDays": 30, "compliancePercentage": 99.873, "errorBudgetRemainingPercentage": -100.0, "errorBudgetRemainingMinutes": -21.6, "errorBudgetTotalMinutes": 21.6, "burnRateOneHour": 0.0, "burnRateSixHours": 0.0, "status": "breached", "sparkline": [100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 96.875, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0, 100.0]}, {"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002af", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002ac", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000065", "applicationName": "Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS)", "serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000068", "serviceName": "benefits-portal", "sliName": "benefits-portal: Synthetic latency", "sliKind": "latency", "isHeadline": false, "isApproximate": false, "targetPercentage": 95.0, "rollingWindowDays": 30, "compliancePercentage": 98.669, "errorBudgetRemainingPercentage": 73.4, "errorBudgetRemainingMinutes": 1585.4, "errorBudgetTotalMinutes": 2160.0, "burnRateOneHour": 0.0, "burnRateSixHours": 0.0, "status": "healthy", "sparkline": [98.611, 98.611, 99.306, 99.653, 98.611, 97.569, 98.611, 98.264, 100.0, 96.875, 98.611, 98.264, 99.653, 98.958, 99.306]}], "stakeholders": [{"displayName": "Aiko AppAdmin", "role": "sre", "preferredLanguageCode": "ja"}], "narrativeMarkdown": "benefits-portal is the primary point of failure (benefits-portal).", "userImpactSummary": "Users of Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS) experience errors or delays in the affected journey."}', N'[{"referenceCode": "K1", "title": "Application topology", "sourceKind": "topology", "knowledgeDocumentId": null}]', N'correct', NULL, N'keigan.admin@keigan.local', NULL, N'cause_not_visible', N'cause_identified', N'nothing_changed_in_checked_sources', N'The SaaS vendor is experiencing degraded performance in its APAC region, which its status page confirms, and our probes see HTTP 503 and multi-second latency.', N'Best supported by direct evidence and timing: The SaaS vendor reports degraded performance in its APAC region.', 12361, 2513, N'["offline-factory"]', N'system:seed', '2026-11-11 06:26:00.000000', '2026-11-11 06:29:00.000000', '2026-11-11 06:26:00.000000', '2026-11-20 12:00:00.000000', N'system:seed', NULL),
    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000358', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000357', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P2, category dependency, 6 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 3 runbook match(es), 6 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 6 service(s) over 107 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 27 evidence items; 10 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 4 direct, 2 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-14 02:22:00.000000', '2026-11-14 04:09:00.000000', '2026-11-14 00:35:00.000000', '2026-11-14 02:22:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P2", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Claims Processing (JP) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "dependency", "candidate_service_names": ["claims-api", "claims-sql"], "incident_summary": "Claims Processing (JP): claim submissions failing with timeouts. Users and systems of Claims Processing (JP) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["claim submissions failing with timeouts"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": true, "final_priority": "P2", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P2"}', N'Claim submissions in Claims Processing (JP) are failing because a recent configuration change overloaded the claims database connections. Customers see long waits and errors when submitting claims. The change can be reverted and the service restarted; recovery is expected within minutes of doing so.', N'Claim submissions on Claims Processing (JP) began failing with timeouts. Error patterns on claims-api that did not exist before the incident ([E2]) show requests waiting for a database connection until they time out, and claims-sql was running at its session limit [E1].', N'A configuration change raised batch import parallelism from 4 to 16 [E9]. Each import thread holds a database connection, so the connection pool of claims-api was exhausted and normal requests queued behind the imports [E2]. claims-sql reached its session limit as a result [E1]. Timing of the change, the first errors and the session growth line up within minutes.', N'Restore the previous batch import concurrency, restart the service to release saturated connections, then cap parallelism below the pool size.

**Step 1. Restore the previous batch import concurrency** (mitigate; medium risk)

Set BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM back to 4 on claims-api (it is 16 now).

Change the setting BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM on claims-api from 16 to 4.

```bash
kubectl set env deployment/claims-api -n claims BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM=4
```

This restarts the service.

This step contains values Keigan assumed and could not verify.

Check: Failed requests return to baseline.

Run the query behind [E6] again.

Expected: No failures within 10 minutes.

Undo: Set the setting back to its previous value.

Change the setting BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM on claims-api from 4 to 16.

**Step 2. Restart the service** (mitigate; medium risk)

Restart claims-api so new pods pick up the corrected configuration.

```bash
kubectl rollout restart deployment/claims-api -n claims
```

Check: Failed requests return to baseline.

Run the query behind [E6] again.

Expected: No failures within 10 minutes.

Undo: Nothing to undo: new instances start from the corrected configuration.

**Step 3. Confirm SQL sessions are falling back** (diagnose; low risk)

Confirm SQL sessions are falling back below 60 percent.

```bash
az monitor metrics list --resource ''/subscriptions/8d1c3f2a-4b6e-4c1d-9a7f-21530c1a0001/resourceGroups/RG_21530_CLMJP_PRD01/providers/Microsoft.Sql/servers/databases/claims-sql'' --metric sessions_percent --interval PT5M --aggregation Maximum
```

Expected: The maximum of sessions_percent stays below 60.

**Step 4. Cap parallelism below the pool size** (durable fix; low risk)

Size the connection pool for peak parallelism and reject configuration where parallelism exceeds the pool.

Check: Confirm the service refuses to start when parallelism exceeds the pool.', N'["Was the change to BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM approved and tested against the SQL session limit?", "Are other services sharing the same database session limit?"]', N'{"schema_version": 2, "overview_markdown": "Restore the previous batch import concurrency, restart the service to release saturated connections, then cap parallelism below the pool size.", "step_references": [{"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-1"}, {"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-2"}, {"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-3"}, {"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-4"}]}', 0.86, N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000384', N'{"nodes": [{"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "serviceName": "claims-api", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015", "serviceName": "claims-sql", "serviceType": "sql_database", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "serviceName": "claims-apim", "serviceType": "api_management", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c", "serviceName": "claims-intake-func", "serviceType": "function_app", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f", "serviceName": "claims-workflow", "serviceType": "logic_app", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "indirect"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012", "serviceName": "claims-nightly-etl", "serviceType": "data_factory", "criticalityTier": "tier_3", "impactLevel": "indirect"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "serviceName": "claims-document-renderer", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "investigated"}], "edges": [{"fromServiceId": "