te_service_names": ["chad-apim"], "incident_summary": "Channel APIs for Digital (AU): mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''. Users and systems of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P3", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P3"}', N'Users of the mobile app in Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are being blocked by a request limit after a new app release started contacting our service far more often. We can raise the limit temporarily and the app team will release a fix.', N'Mobile app users of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) see "too many requests" when opening the policy summary. The gateway returned HTTP 429 at a much higher rate than before [E3] [E2].', N'Request volume to the policy summary operation rose about fourfold [E1], consistent with a mobile release that polls every 5 seconds instead of 60. The API Management rate-limit policy then rejected requests over quota with 429 [E2].', N'Raise the rate limit temporarily to stop user-facing 429 responses, then restore the 60 second polling interval in the mobile app.

**Step 1. Raise the rate limit temporarily** (mitigate; medium risk)

Raise the per-subscription limit in the inbound policy of the mobile policy-summary operation (change process applies).

Check: 429 responses drop.

Run the query behind [E3] again.

Expected: Below 1 percent.

Undo: Restore the previous policy revision of the API in API Management.

**Step 2. Ship the mobile hot-fix** (durable fix; low risk)

Ship the mobile hot-fix that restores the 60 second polling interval and add client-side back-off on 429.

Check: Confirm request volume per subscription returns to the baseline rate.

**Step 3. Restore the original rate limit** (mitigate; low risk)

After the hot-fix reaches most users, restore the original rate limit.

Check: Confirm 429 responses stay below 1 percent.', N'["Which mobile app version introduced the polling interval change?", "Is a staged rollout of the fix available?"]', N'{"schema_version": 2, "overview_markdown": "Raise the rate limit temporarily to stop user-facing 429 responses, then restore the 60 second polling interval in the mobile app.", "step_references": [{"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-1"}, {"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-2"}, {"perspective": "application", "step_id": "application-3"}]}', 0.68, N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003c1', N'{"nodes": [{"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002e", "serviceName": "chad-apim", "serviceType": "api_management", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000032", "serviceName": "channel-gateway-app", "serviceType": "app_service", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "investigated"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002f", "serviceName": "azaustaekub14470pr0101", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "investigated"}], "edges": [{"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002e", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000032", "kind": "calls"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002e", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002f", "kind": "calls"}], "impactedSlos": [{"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000267", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000264", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029", "applicationName": "Channel APIs for Digital (AU)", "serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002e", "serviceName": "chad-apim", "sliName": "chad-apim: Gateway availability", "sliKind": "availability", "isHeadline": true, "isApproximate": false, "targetPercentage": 99.5, "rollingWindowDays": 30, "compliancePercentage": 99.842, "errorBudgetRemainingPercentage": 68.4, "errorBudgetRemainingMinutes": 147.7, "errorBudgetTotalMinutes": 216.0, "burnRateOneHour": 0.75, "burnRateSixHours": 0.76, "status": "healthy", "sparkline": [99.93, 99.925, 99.924, 99.927, 99.924, 99.926, 99.928, 99.925, 99.928, 99.804, 98.869, 99.618, 99.616, 99.616, 99.619]}, {"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000269", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000266", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029", "applicationName": "Channel APIs for Digital (AU)", "serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000002e", "serviceName": "chad-apim", "sliName": "chad-apim: Gateway latency", "sliKind": "latency", "isHeadline": false, "isApproximate": true, "targetPercentage": 95.0, "rollingWindowDays": 30, "compliancePercentage": 98.506, "errorBudgetRemainingPercentage": 70.1, "errorBudgetRemainingMinutes": 1514.2, "errorBudgetTotalMinutes": 2160.0, "burnRateOneHour": 0.22, "burnRateSixHours": 0.31, "status": "healthy", "sparkline": [98.492, 98.588, 98.531, 98.211, 98.495, 98.507, 98.473, 98.507, 98.446, 98.561, 98.353, 98.5, 98.401, 98.312, 98.629]}], "stakeholders": [{"displayName": "Kai Admin", "role": "lead", "preferredLanguageCode": "en"}, {"displayName": "Aiko AppAdmin", "role": "developer", "preferredLanguageCode": "ja"}], "narrativeMarkdown": "chad-apim is the primary point of failure (chad-apim).", "userImpactSummary": "Users of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) experience errors or delays in the affected journey."}', N'[{"referenceCode": "K1", "title": "Application topology", "sourceKind": "topology", "knowledgeDocumentId": null}, {"referenceCode": "K2", "title": "Channel APIs cluster code context", "sourceKind": "document_digest", "knowledgeDocumentId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000089"}, {"referenceCode": "K3", "title": "Channel APIs cluster code context", "sourceKind": "document_chunk", "knowledgeDocumentId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000089"}, {"referenceCode": "K4", "title": "Channel APIs cluster code context", "sourceKind": "document_chunk", "knowledgeDocumentId": "0000