    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003df', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003de', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P3, category dependency, 4 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 1 runbook match(es), 4 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 4 service(s) over 129 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 18 evidence items; 8 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 2 direct, 2 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-17 04:19:00.000000', '2026-11-17 06:28:00.000000', '2026-11-17 02:10:00.000000', '2026-11-17 04:19:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P3", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Payments Platform (AU) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "dependency", "candidate_service_names": ["payment-confirmation-func", "payments-apim"], "incident_summary": "Payments Platform (AU): payment confirmations delayed. Users and systems of Payments Platform (AU) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["payment confirmations delayed"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P3", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P3"}', N'Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed because our partner bank''s service is responding very slowly. Payments are not lost but confirmations arrive late. We are engaging the partner and changing how our system retries so it does not add load.', N'Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed by minutes. Outbound calls to the partner payment gateway time out after about 25 seconds [E3], and dependency failures to that target are new [E7].', N'The partner bank gateway slowed down. payment-confirmation-func retries each call up to five times without jitter, which amplifies load and exhausts the outbound HTTP client pool [E3]. The partner slowdown is the trigger; the retry design makes the effect worse and longer.', N'Stop amplifying the partner slowdown: enable the circuit-breaker fallback, add jitter to retries and engage the partner.

**Step 1. Check the partner endpoint latency** (diagnose; low risk)

Check the partner endpoint latency from a trusted host (read-only).

Run the query behind [E3] again.

Expected: Latency is back below the timeout.

**Step 2. Enable the circuit-breaker fallback** (mitigate; medium risk)

Enable the payment gateway circuit-breaker fallback so confirmations are queued instead of retried synchronously.

Check: Outbound HTTP client pool usage falls.

Run the query behind [E3] again.

Expected: Pool usage below 70 percent.

Undo: Disable the fallback queue once the partner is healthy and drain deferred confirmations.

**Step 3. Engage the partner** (mitigate; low risk)

Raise the incident with the partner bank''s operations contact and share the timeout timestamps from the evidence.

No check was given for this step.', N'["Has the partner acknowledged a degradation on their side?", "Are deferred confirmations queued durably so none are lost?"]', N'{"schema_version": 2, "overview_markdown": "Stop amplifying the partner slowdown: enable the circuit-breaker fallback, add jitter to retries and engage the partner.", "step_references": [{"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-1"}, {"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-2"}, {"perspective": "dependencies", "step_id": "dependencies-3"}]}', 0.84, N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ff', N'{"nodes": [{"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000047", "serviceName": "payment-confirmation-func", "serviceType": "function_app", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000004a", "serviceName": "payments-apim", "serviceType": "api_management", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000046", "serviceName": "payment-api", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "indirect"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000050", "serviceName": "syd-f5-ltm-01", "serviceType": "network_appliance", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "indirect"}], "edges": [{"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000004a", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000046", "kind": "calls"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000046", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000047", "kind": "publishes_to"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000047", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000004a", "kind": "calls"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000050", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000004a", "kind": "hosted_on"}], "impactedSlos": [{"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000290", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000028d", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-40