ory limit and are killed by the kernel [E4]. Memory grows by roughly 300 MB per hour, which indicates a leak in the document renderer rather than a one-off spike. While pods restart the gateway has no healthy backend and returns 502.", "fix_overview_markdown": "Relieve memory pressure with a temporary limit increase and restart; fix the renderer''s unreleased image buffers.", "recommended_fix_steps": [{"perspective": "infrastructure", "step_number": 1}, {"perspective": "infrastructure", "step_number": 2}, {"perspective": "infrastructure", "step_number": 3}, {"perspective": "infrastructure", "step_number": 4}], "open_questions": ["Which release introduced the memory growth?", "Can the renderer be load tested with a memory profile before the next release?"], "applied_runbook_codes": ["R1"]}', 1805, 0, N'12ac2c18b4778a25dde10c5c4c812cf6b46d83791a3b96237e580a8bc5d12467', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
