    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000323', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002f5', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002f6', N'Postmortem: Channel APIs for Digital (AU): all calls to the policy core system failing', N'# Postmortem: Channel APIs for Digital (AU): all calls to the policy core system failing

## Summary

A security certificate that Channel APIs for Digital (AU) uses to talk to the policy core system expired at midnight UTC, so most calls fail. A new certificate must be issued and loaded; service returns once it is in place.

## Impact

Channel APIs for Digital (AU) was degraded for 25 minutes. Calls from Channel APIs for Digital (AU) to the policy core system fail with TLS errors, so channel API operations that need policy data are unavailable [E2].

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
| --- | --- |
| 2026-11-07 05:29 UTC | Incident INC004090274 opened in ServiceNow |
| 2026-11-07 05:30 UTC | Keigan started investigating |
| 2026-11-07 05:32 UTC | Evidence collected: 10 items, 5 strong |
| 2026-11-07 05:33 UTC | Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 88%) |
| 2026-11-07 05:49 UTC | Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied |
| 2026-11-07 05:54 UTC | Incident resolved |

## Root cause

The mutual-TLS client certificate used to call the policy core system expired at 00:00 UTC. The first failure appears at that moment and the error text states that the certificate has expired [E2]. No change was deployed, which fits a time-based cause.

## Contributing factors

- Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.
- The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check.

## Detection

The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.

## Response

Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 25 minutes.

## What went well

- Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.
- Stakeholders received bilingual updates early.

## What could be improved

- Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.
- The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed.

## Action items
| Action | Owner role | Due | Type | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Automate certificate renewal and rotation in Key Vault | developer | 2026-12-07 | prevent | top |
| Alert 30, 14 and 7 days before any certificate expires | lead | 2026-11-14 | detect | normal |
| Document the emergency issuance path and its approvers | developer | 2026-11-21 | mitigate | normal |

## Lessons learned

