ot cause hypothesis before responders joined.", "Stakeholders received bilingual updates early."], "what_could_be_improved": ["Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.", "The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed."], "action_items": [{"description": "Negotiate a vendor SLA with regional failover and incident notification commitments", "owner_role": "Vendor management", "due_in_days": 60, "action_type": "prevent", "priority": "top"}, {"description": "Subscribe operations to the vendor status feed so incidents are known within minutes", "owner_role": "Benefits SRE team", "due_in_days": 7, "action_type": "detect", "priority": "normal"}, {"description": "Prepare a standard employee notice template for vendor outages", "owner_role": "Benefits platform team", "due_in_days": 14, "action_type": "mitigate", "priority": "normal"}], "lessons_learned": ["For vendor-hosted services, detection and communication are our main levers."], "incident_resolved_at": "2026-11-11T07:39:00+00:00"}', N'en', N'final', N'seed', N'keigan.admin@keigan.local', '2026-11-12 07:39:00.000000', '2026-11-12 07:44:00.000000', '2026-11-11 08:39:00.000000', '2026-11-20 12:00:00.000000', N'system:seed', NULL),
    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000039b', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000357', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000358', N'Postmortem: Claims Processing (JP): claim submissions failing with timeouts', N'# Postmortem: Claims Processing (JP): claim submissions failing with timeouts

## Summary

Claim submissions in Claims Processing (JP) are failing because a recent configuration change overloaded the claims database connections. Customers see long waits and errors when submitting claims. The change can be reverted and the service restarted; recovery is expected within minutes of doing so.

## Impact

Claims Processing (JP) was degraded for 42 minutes. Claim submissions on Claims Processing (JP) began failing with timeouts. Error patterns on claims-api that did not exist before the incident ([E2]) show requests waiting for a database connection until they time out, and claims-sql was running at its session limit [E1].

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
| --- | --- |
| 2026-11-14 01:10 UTC | Routine release 2026.11.14.1 deployed |
| 2026-11-14 03:09 UTC | App setting BATCH_IMPORT_PARALLELISM changed from 4 to 16 (release 2026.11.18.2) |
| 2026-11-14 03:22 UTC | Incident INC004090000 opened in ServiceNow |
| 2026-11-14 03:23 UTC | Keigan started investigating |
| 2026-11-14 03:25 UTC | Evidence collected: 27 items, 10 strong |
| 2026-11-14 03:26 UTC | Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 86%) |
| 2026-11-14 03:42 UTC | Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied |
| 2026-11-14 04:04 UTC | Incident resolved |
| 2026-11-20 12:00 UTC | The incident text contained instruction-like content, which Keigan ignored |

## Root cause

A configuration change raised batch import parallelism from 4 to 16 [E9]. Each import thread holds a database connection, so the connection pool of claims-api was exhausted and normal requests queued behind the imports [E2]. claims-sql reached its session limit as a result [E1]. Timing of the change, the first errors and the session growth line up within minutes.

## Contributing factors

- Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.
- The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check.

## Detection

The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.

## Response

Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 42 minutes.

## What went well

- Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.
- Stakeholders received bilingual updates early.

## What could be improved

- Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.
- The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed.

## Action items
| Action | Owner role | Due | Type | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Add a startup validation that rejects batch parallelism greater than the connection pool size | lead | 2026-11-28 | prevent | top |
| Alert when SQL sessions exceed 80 percent for 5 minutes | manager | 2026-11-21 | detect | normal |
| Document and rehearse reverting configuration releases within 10 minutes | infra | 2026-12-05 | mitigate | normal |

## Lessons learned

