    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003d8', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003a1', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003a2', N'Postmortem: Channel APIs for Digital (AU): mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''', N'# Postmortem: Channel APIs for Digital (AU): mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''

## Summary

Users of the mobile app in Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are being blocked by a request limit after a new app release started contacting our service far more often. We can raise the limit temporarily and the app team will release a fix.

## Impact

Channel APIs for Digital (AU) was degraded for 49 minutes. Mobile app users of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) see "too many requests" when opening the policy summary. The gateway returned HTTP 429 at a much higher rate than before [E3] [E2].

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
| --- | --- |
| 2026-11-16 01:10 UTC | Routine release 2026.11.16.1 deployed |
| 2026-11-16 06:20 UTC | Incident INC004090411 opened in ServiceNow |
| 2026-11-16 06:21 UTC | Keigan started investigating |
| 2026-11-16 06:23 UTC | Evidence collected: 17 items, 4 strong |
| 2026-11-16 06:24 UTC | Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 68%) |
| 2026-11-16 06:40 UTC | Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied |
| 2026-11-16 07:09 UTC | Incident resolved |

## Root cause

Request volume to the policy summary operation rose about fourfold [E1], consistent with a mobile release that polls every 5 seconds instead of 60. The API Management rate-limit policy then rejected requests over quota with 429 [E2].

## Contributing factors

- Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.
- The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check.

## Detection

The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.

## Response

Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 49 minutes.

## What went well

- Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.
- Stakeholders received bilingual updates early.

## What could be improved

- Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.
- The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed.

## Action items
| Action | Owner role | Due | Type | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Add client-side back-off on HTTP 429 in the mobile app | developer | 2026-11-30 | prevent | top |
| Alert on a sudden rise in per-subscription request rate | lead | 2026-11-23 | detect | normal |
| Document how to raise API Management rate limits safely | developer | 2026-11-30 | mitigate | normal |

## Lessons learned

- Client release notes should state any change in polling or request frequency.', N'{"report_title": "Postmortem: Channel APIs for Digital (AU): mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''", "summary": "Users of the mobile app in Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are being blocked by a request limit after a new app release started contacting our service far more often. We can raise the limit temporarily and the app team will release a fix.", "impact": "Channel APIs for Digital (AU) was degraded for 49 minutes. Mobile app users of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) see \"too many requests\" when opening the policy summary. The gateway returned HTTP 429 at a much higher rate than before [E3] [E2].", "timeline": [{"time_text": "2026-11-16 01:10 UTC", "description": "Routine release 2026.11.16.1 deployed"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 06:20 UTC", "description": "Incident INC004090411 opened in ServiceNow"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 06:21 UTC", "description": "Keigan started investigating"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 06:23 UTC", "description": "Evidence collected: 17 items, 4 strong"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 06:24 UTC", "description": "Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 68%)"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 06:40 UTC", "description": "Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-16 07:09 UTC", "description": "Incident resolved"}], "root_cause": "Request volume to the policy summary operation rose about fourfold [E1], consistent with a mobile release that polls every 5 seconds instead of 60. The API Management rate-limit policy then rejected requests over quota with 429 [E2].", "contributing_factors": ["Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.", "The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check."], "detection": "The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.", "response": "Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 49 minutes.", "what_went_well": ["Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.", "Stakeholders received bilingual updates early."], "what_could_be_improved": ["Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.", "The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed."], "action_items": [{"description": "Add client-side back-off on HTTP 429 in the mobile app", "owner_role": "Mobile app team", "due_in_days": 14, "action_type": "prevent", "priority": "top"}, {"description": "Alert on a sudden rise in per-subscription request rate", "owner_role": "Channel SRE team", "due_in_days": 7, "action_type": "detect", "priority": "normal"}, {"description": "Document how to raise API Management rate limits safely", "owner_role": "Channel platform team", "due_in_days": 14, "action_type": "mitigate", "priority": "normal"}], "lessons_learned": ["Client release notes should state any change in polling or request frequency."], "incident_resolved_at": "2026-11-16T07:09:00+00:00"}', N'en', N'final', N'seed', N'keigan.admin@keigan.local', '2026-11-17 07:09:00.000000', '2026-11-17 07:14:00.000000', '2026-11-16 08:09:00.000000', '2026-11-20 12:00:00.000000', N'system:seed', NULL),
    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000415', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003de', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000003df', N'Postmortem: Payments Platform (AU): payment confirmations delayed', N'# Postmortem: Payments Platform (AU): payment confirmations delayed

## Summary

Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed because our partner bank''s service is responding very slowly. Payments are not lost but confirmations arrive late. We are engaging the partner and changing how our system retries so it does not add load.

## Impact

Payments Platform (AU) was degraded for 64 minutes. Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed by minutes. Outbound calls to the partner payment gateway time out after about 25 seconds [E3], and dependency failures to that target are new [E7].

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
| --- | --- |
| 2026-11-17 05:19 UTC | Incident INC004090548 opened in ServiceNow |
| 2026-11-17 05:20 UTC | Keigan started investigating |
| 2026-11-17 05:22 UTC | Evidence collected: 18 items, 8 strong |
| 2026-11-17 05:23 UTC | Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 84%) |
| 2026-11-17 05:39 UTC | Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied |
| 2026-11-17 06:23 UTC | Incident resolved |

## Root cause

The partner bank gateway slowed down. payment-confirmation-func retries each call up to five times without jitter, which amplifies load and exhausts the outbound HTTP client pool [E3]. The partner slowdown is the trigger; the retry design makes the effect worse and longer.

## Contributing factors

- Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.
- The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check.

## Detection

The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.

## Response

Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 64 minutes.

## What went well

- Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.
- Stakeholders received bilingual updates early.

## What could be improved

- Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.
- The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed.

## Action items

| Action | Owner role | Due | Type | Priority |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Add jitter and a total retry budget to the payment gateway client | Payments platform team | 2026-12-01 | prevent | top |
| Alert on partner call latency p95 above 10 seconds | Payments SRE team | 2026-11-24 | detect | normal |
| Add a circuit-breaker fallback that queues confirmations | Payments platform team | 2026-12-17 | mitigate | normal |

## Lessons learned

- Retries are load; unbounded retries convert a partner slowdown into our own outage.', N'{"report_title": "Postmortem: Payments Platform (AU): payment confirmations delayed", "summary": "Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed because our partner bank''s service is responding very slowly. Payments are not lost but confirmations arrive late. We are engaging the partner and changing how our system retries so it does not add load.", "impact": "Payments Platform (AU) was degraded for 64 minutes. Payment confirmations in Payments Platform (AU) are delayed by minutes. Outbound calls to the partner payment gateway time out after about 25 seconds [E3], and dependency failures to that target are new [E7].", "timeline": [{"time_text": "2026-11-17 05:19 UTC", "description": "Incident INC004090548 opened in ServiceNow"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-17 05:20 UTC", "description": "Keigan started investigating"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-17 05:22 UTC", "description": "Evidence collected: 18 items, 8 strong"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-17 05:23 UTC", "description": "Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 84%)"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-17 05:39 UTC", "description": "Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-17 06:23 UTC", "description": "Incident resolved"}], "root_cause": "The partner bank gateway slowed down. payment-confirmation-func retries each call up to five times without jitter, which amplifies load and exhausts the outbound HTTP client pool [E3]. The partner slowdown is the trigger; the retry design makes the effect worse and longer.", "contributing_factors": ["Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.", "The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check."], "detection": "The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.", "response": "Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 64 minutes.", "what_went_well": ["Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.", "Stakeholders received bilingual updates early."], "what_could_be_improved": ["Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.", "The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed."], "action_items": [{"description": "Add jitter and a total retry budget to the payment gateway client", "owner_role": "Payments platform team", "due_in_days": 14, "action_type": "prevent", "priority": "top"}, {"description": "Alert on partner call latency p95 above 10 seconds", "owner_role": "Payments SRE team", "due_in_days": 7, "action_type": "detect", "priority": "normal"}, {"description": "Add a circuit-breaker fallback that queues confirmations", "owner_role": "Payments platform team", "due_in_days": 30, "action_type": "mitigate", "priority": "normal"}], "lessons_learned": ["Retries are load; unbounded retries convert a partner slowdown into our own outage."], "incident_resolved_at": "2026-11-17T06:23:00+00:00"}', N'en', N'draft', N'seed', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-17 07:23:00.000000', '2026-11-20 12:00:00.000000', N'system:seed', NULL),
    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000445', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000041b', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000041c', N'Postmortem: Policy Administration Mainframe (US): nightly premium billing batch did not complete', N'# Postmortem: Policy Administration Mainframe (US): nightly premium billing batch did not complete

## Summary

The nightly premium billing run in Policy Administration Mainframe (US) stopped part-way because one input record is malformed. Statements for the billing cycle are delayed until the record is corrected and the job is restarted from the failed step.

## Impact

Policy Administration Mainframe (US) was degraded for 89 minutes. The nightly premium billing batch for Policy Administration Mainframe (US) did not complete: job PBIL0400 abended in step STEP030 [E1], so downstream statements were not produced.

## Timeline

| Time | Event |
| --- | --- |
| 2026-11-18 01:10 UTC | Routine release 2026.11.18.1 deployed |
| 2026-11-18 04:18 UTC | Incident INC004090685 opened in ServiceNow |
| 2026-11-18 04:19 UTC | Keigan started investigating |
| 2026-11-18 04:21 UTC | Evidence collected: 5 items, 3 strong |
| 2026-11-18 04:22 UTC | Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 85%) |
| 2026-11-18 04:38 UTC | Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied |
| 2026-11-18 05:47 UTC | Incident resolved |

## Root cause

PBIL0400 abended with S0C7, a data exception, in program PBILCALC [E1]. This happens when the program does arithmetic on a field that is not valid packed decimal, most likely a malformed premium amount in the input data set.

## Contributing factors

- Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.
- The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check.

## Detection

The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collected evidence within minutes.

## Response

Responders followed the investigation''s proposed fix. Total time to restore service: 89 minutes.

## What went well

- Keigan assembled evidence and a ranked root cause hypothesis before responders joined.
- Stakeholders received bilingual updates early.

## What could be improved

- Detection depended on a user-visible symptom; an earlier signal would shorten time to detect.
- The fix steps were manual and should be rehearsed.

## Action items

| Action | Owner role | Due | Type | Priority |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Validate packed-decimal fields in the input extract before the billing job starts | Premium billing team | 2026-12-09 | prevent | top |
| Alert operations within 5 minutes of any ABEND in the billing chain | Mainframe operations | 2026-11-25 | detect | normal |
| Document the restart procedure from STEP030 including data correction approval | Premium billing team | 2026-12-02 | mitigate | normal |

## Lessons learned

- Data validation at the start of the batch chain is cheaper than a restart at 3 a.m.', N'{"report_title": "Postmortem: Policy Administration Mainframe (US): nightly premium billing batch did not complete", "summary": "The nightly premium billing run in Policy Administration Mainframe (US) stopped part-way because one input record is malformed. Statements for the billing cycle are delayed until the record is corrected and the job is restarted from the failed step.", "impact": "Policy Administration Mainframe (US) was degraded for 89 minutes. The nightly premium billing batch for Policy Administration Mainframe (US) did not complete: job PBIL0400 abended in step STEP030 [E1], so downstream statements were not produced.", "timeline": [{"time_text": "2026-11-18 01:10 UTC", "description": "Routine release 2026.11.18.1 deployed"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 04:18 UTC", "description": "Incident INC004090685 opened in ServiceNow"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 04:19 UTC", "description": "Keigan started investigating"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 04:21 UTC", "description": "Evidence collected: 5 items, 3 strong"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 04:22 UTC", "description": "Root cause analysis ready: cause identified (confidence 85%)"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 04:38 UTC", "description": "Responder confirmed the proposed fix was applied"}, {"time_text": "2026-11-18 05:47 UTC", "description": "Incident resolved"}], "root_cause": "PBIL0400 abended with S0C7, a data exception, in program PBILCALC [E1]. This happens when the program does arithmetic on a field that is not valid packed decimal, most likely a malformed premium amount in the input data set.", "contributing_factors": ["Existing alerts did not describe the failing component clearly enough to shorten diagnosis.", "The relevant limit or dependency was not covered by a capacity or readiness check."], "detection": "The incident was raised in ServiceNow and picked up by Keigan, which started the investigation immediately and collect